---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is it really free?",
    a: "The app is free to download and dictate locally on your Mac — no trial, no account. There's also an optional cloud model you can switch on for tougher audio, billed by the second with no subscription. You only ever pay if you choose to use it."
  },
  {
    q: "How fast is it?",
    a: "In local mode, by the time you've let go of the key your words are at the cursor. No upload, no spinner."
  },
  {
    q: "How accurate is it?",
    a: "Local is noticeably better than built-in Mac dictation, and you can add your own vocabulary and shortcuts. For noisy rooms, accents, and heavy jargon, the optional cloud model is a clear step up."
  },
  {
    q: "Does it work offline?",
    a: "Local mode does. After a one-time model download on first launch, no internet is needed. The optional cloud model needs a connection, since it sends audio to the provider."
  },
  {
    q: "What leaves my Mac, and when?",
    a: "In local mode — the default — nothing leaves your Mac; transcription runs entirely on-device. In cloud mode, which you turn on yourself, the audio you choose to send goes to the model provider (OpenAI at launch) and nothing else. The switch is explicit, shows a distinct menu-bar state, and never happens silently."
  },
  {
    q: "Can WhisperFree employees hear my audio?",
    a: "No. In cloud mode your audio goes straight to the model provider for transcription. On our side we only ever see metering data — duration, timestamps, and your credit balance — never your audio or the text."
  },
  {
    q: "What does OpenAI do with my audio?",
    a: "OpenAI retains API audio for up to 30 days for abuse monitoring, then deletes it, and doesn't train on it. We can't offer a zero-retention guarantee at launch, so we're saying so plainly rather than burying it. Local mode avoids this entirely."
  },
  {
    q: "Why trust this from an app built on “stays on your Mac”?",
    a: "Because cloud is off by default and only runs when you switch it on, with a visible menu-bar state. Local mode is unchanged: free, private, and on by default. Cloud is an option for the cases where local struggles — not a change to how the app behaves unless you ask for it."
  },
  {
    q: "What languages are supported?",
    a: "English only for now. More languages later."
  },
  {
    q: "Is it open source?",
    a: "Not currently. The app is free to download and built on open-source voice models."
  },
  {
    q: "How is this different from built-in Mac dictation?",
    a: "It's faster, more accurate, and you can teach it. Add your vocabulary and write your own auto-corrections so it gets your names, jargon, and quirks right. Built-in dictation does none of that."
  },
  {
    q: "How does this compare to Wispr Flow, Superwhisper, or Aqua Voice?",
    a: "Wispr Flow and Aqua Voice are paid cloud subscriptions — fast and polished, but your audio always leaves your Mac and you pay every month. Superwhisper is on-device like us, but paid. WhisperFree runs locally for free, and adds an optional pay-by-the-second cloud model only when you want the extra accuracy — so you're never locked into a subscription."
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="py-20 px-6 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12">Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      {faqs.map(({ q, a }) => (
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="px-6 py-4 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900 flex items-center justify-between list-none">
            {q}
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 shrink-0 ml-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
              <path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-gray-600">
            {a}
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
